{"entryId":"3425","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3425:1","sourceSha256":"a1b915eccaaf2712c7a53706f4c5bdb5145633d4ea4a530815e5d8b80c5bfac7","englishSha256":"4528596c1af374f7c9952ac7aec1d2d8f849ccceeba69da510b4132bd3c01a7c","citations":[{"id":"3425:1:link-001","he":[17,30],"en":[32,61],"target":{"entry":131,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 131:1","assessment":"The Avtolas and Ezra entries preserve different generations and readings. The cross-reference records Heilprin’s genealogy with those variants.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 131:1","target":{"entry":131,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2874:1","target":{"entry":2874,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Menachot 53a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_53a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3425:1:link-002","he":[149,176],"en":[296,332],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_21a.16"},"reference":"Sotah 21a:16","assessment":"Ulla expressly cites the case of Shimon and Azaryah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 21a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_21a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3425:1:link-003","he":[177,188],"en":[334,349],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_21a.16.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 21a:16:1","assessment":"Rashi explains the commercial patronage, sharing in the merit of study, and why Shimon bears his brother’s name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 21a:16:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_21a.16.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3425:1:link-004","he":[197,216],"en":[365,400],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Zevachim_1.2"},"reference":"Mishnah Zevachim 1:2","assessment":"Rashi’s phrase refers to the opening of Zevahim. The standard division gives the explicit Shimon citation as the second mishnah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Zevachim 1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Zevachim_1.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 21a:16:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_21a.16.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3425:1:link-005","he":[234,293],"en":[428,541],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_25.2"},"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 25:2","assessment":"Vayikra Rabbah supplies the direct verbal parallel explaining attribution by financial support.","evidence":[{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 25:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_25.2"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"3425:1:link-006","he":[295,302],"en":[543,560],"target":{"entry":1033,"paragraph":6},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1033:6","assessment":"The Hillel entry contrasts his and Shevna’s later proposal with Shimon and Azaryah’s prior arrangement.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1033:6","target":{"entry":1033,"paragraph":6},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3425:1:link-007","he":[412,430],"en":[745,777],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tahorot_8.7"},"reference":"Mishnah Tahorot 8:7","assessment":"Tohorot 8:7 expressly names Shimon in a dispute on liquids and impurity. The anomalous prefix is preserved in the Hebrew witness.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Tahorot 8:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tahorot_8.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"holds":[{"raw":"הכהן דודו של ר\"א בן עזריה","reason":"Heilprin’s uncle and priestly genealogy depends on the competing readings discussed in his Ezra entry.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2876:1","target":{"entry":2876,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Menachot 53a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_53a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ובילמדנו קדושים","reason":"The matching homily is available in Vayikra Rabbah. The Yelammedenu attribution itself has yet to be localized in a direct witness.","evidence":[{"reference":"Vayikra Rabbah 25:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Vayikra_Rabbah_25.2"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"raw":"גם אחיו חכם גדול ונכבד בבית הכהנים תשיעי לעזרא","reason":"The generation count presupposes one of the genealogical readings. The Bavli expressly describes Elazar as tenth from Ezra and preserves a different descent line for the visitor to Peridah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 53a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_53a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2874:1","target":{"entry":2874,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"raw":"כתב הרמב\"ם לא נזכר במשנה כ\"א פ\"א דזבחים משנה ב'","reason":"The statement’s attributed Rambam locus remains unlocalized. The cited Zevahim and additional Tohorot references both name Shimon explicitly.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Zevachim 1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Zevachim_1.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Tahorot 8:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tahorot_8.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]}],"notes":[],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Zevachim 1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Zevachim_1.2"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 21a:16:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_21a.16.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Mishnah Tahorot 8:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Tahorot_8.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
